  "job_B2.2.8_20251003_114504": {
    "text": "HER ONGYN\u00f0 BE CRISTENDOME.\nLeofan men, eallum cristenum mannum is mycel \u00feearf \u00fe\u00e6t hy heora cristendomes gescad witan, & \u00fe\u00e6t\nBe Cristes agenum naman syn cristene genamode, for\u00f0am Crist is cristenra heafod, & ealle cristene men\nLytel frema\u00f0 \u00feeah cristen nama butan cristenum d\u00e6dum, ac se bi\u00f0 rihtlice cristen \u00fee Cristes larum & his\nSe \u00fee secge \u00fe\u00e6t he on Crist gelyfe, fare se \u00fe\u00e6s rihtweges \u00fee Crist sylf ferde.\nAnd \u00f0eah hwa cwe\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t he on Crist rihtlice gelyfe & nele his larum ne his lagum folgian, he lih\u00f0 him\nGyf ge me lufian, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, folgia\u00f0 minum larum, for\u00f0am se me ne lufia\u00f0 na \u00fee nele minum larum\nNu age we \u00feearfe \u00fee cristene syndon \u00fe\u00e6t we georne his larum & his lagum fyligean.\nLeofan men, hit gewear\u00f0 on geardagum \u00fe\u00e6t God sylf sp\u00e6c hludre stefne of Synai Munte to Moyse \u00feam\nIc eom \u00f0in Drihten, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fee gel\u00e6dde \u00fee ut of Egyptum.\nNe weor\u00f0a \u00feu fremde godas.\nNe \u00feu \u00feines Drihtnes naman ne namie on idel.\nWite \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u \u00fe\u00e6ne rested\u00e6g freolsige georne.\nWeor\u00f0a geornlice f\u00e6der & modor.\nNe beo \u00f0u \u00e6nig manslaga.\nNe afyl \u00fee mid forligere.\nNe scea\u00fea \u00f0u.\nNe leoh \u00feu.\nNe gyrn \u00f0u o\u00f0res mannes wifes, ne \u00e6niges \u00feinges \u00fee o\u00f0er man age ne gyrn \u00feu on unriht.\n\u00d0as tyn beboda God sylf gedihte & awrat & Moyse bef\u00e6ste; & Crist on his godspelle eft hy\n\u00d0\u00e6t is rihtlic lagu, & se bi\u00f0 ges\u00e6lig se \u00fee hy gehealde\u00f0.\n\u00deas beboda & fela hertoeacan we sculon healdan, be \u00feam \u00fee us Cristes bec gelomlice l\u00e6ra\u00f0, gif we\nEala, leofan men, us is swy\u00f0e mycel \u00feearf \u00fe\u00e6t we ofer ealle o\u00f0re \u00feing God huru lufian & his larum &\nEalle we habba\u00f0 \u00e6nne heofonlicne f\u00e6der & ane gastlice modor, seo is ecclesia genamod, \u00fe\u00e6t is Godes\nLa hw\u00e6t, frema\u00f0 cyrichatan cristendom on unnyt, for\u00f0am \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra bi\u00f0 Godes feond \u00fee bi\u00f0 Godes\nAnd egeslice sp\u00e6c Gregorius be \u00f0am \u00fea \u00f0a he \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: si quis ecclesiam Dei denudauerit uel\nSe \u00f0e Godes cyrican, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, rype o\u00f0\u00f0e reafige o\u00f0\u00f0e halignessa gri\u00f0 scyrde o\u00f0\u00f0e wyrde, a he\nEala, rihte gedafena\u00f0 cristenum mannum \u00fe\u00e6t hi Crist sylfne geefenl\u00e6can georne, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e hy don\n\u00d0\u00e6t is, \u00fe\u00e6t gehwa georne unriht forl\u00e6te & inwerdre heortan hwyrfe to rihte for Gode & for worulde.\nLa, hu m\u00e6g man ea\u00f0ost gehwyrfan fram yfele & fram unrihte, butan \u00fe\u00e6t man deofol georne forbuge &\n\u00d0\u00e6t is gitsung & gifernes, galnes & weamodnys, unrotnys & asolcennys, gylpgeornys & ofermodignys.\nOf \u00f0yson eahta deofles cr\u00e6ftan ealle un\u00feeawas up aspringa\u00f0 & sy\u00f0\u00fean tobr\u00e6da\u00f0 ealles to wide.\n\u00d0onne syndon eahta healice m\u00e6gnu \u00feurh Godes mihte mannum gescyte: \u00f0\u00e6t is rumheortnys &\nMid \u00feysan m\u00e6genan we us sculon werian & \u00f0urh Godes fultum deofol oferwinnan & his un\u00feeawan\nLeofan men, ure Drihten sp\u00e6c to Moyse hwilum & be \u00f0\u00e6re gitsunge \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Non concupiscas ullam\nNe gyrn \u00f0u on unriht, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00e6niges \u00feinges \u00fee o\u00f0er man age, & se apostol cw\u00e6\u00f0: radix omnium\nGitsung is wyrtruma, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00e6ghwylces yfeles.\nLeofan men, do\u00f0 swa ic l\u00e6re, scylda\u00f0 wi\u00f0 \u00fea gitsunge \u00e6fre swy\u00f0e georne & warnia\u00f0 eac symle wi\u00f0\n\u00d0urh gifernesse Adam forlet \u00e6rest paradisum.\nAnd eac ic l\u00e6re georne manna gehwylcne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6nig ne afyle mid fulan forligere \u00e6fre hine sylfne.\nNe \u00e6nig ne healde yrre on his heortan ealles to lange.\nNe \u00e6nig \u00f0urh worldhoge forsorgie to swy\u00f0e, ac hihte on his Drihten.\nNe \u00e6fre \u00e6nig man idelnesse lufige ealles to gelome.\nNe \u00e6fre \u00e6nig man unnyt lof & idel gylp lufige to swy\u00f0e.\nNe \u00e6fre \u00e6nig man ofermetta lufie, ac \u00e6fre hy ascunie.\nAnd scylde man eac wi\u00f0 mansliht \u00e6fre swy\u00f0e georne, & scylde man wi\u00f0 galnysse & wi\u00f0 \u00e6wbryce\nUnrihte gemeta & woge gewihta aweorpe man georne, & \u00e6fre \u00e6nig man o\u00f0rum ne swicie ealles to\nNe \u00e6nig man o\u00f0erne to nearwe ne h\u00e6fte ne on unriht ne ge\u00feeowige.\nNe \u00e6nig man \u00feurh reaflac o\u00f0erne ne rype.\nNe \u00e6nig man o\u00f0erne on unriht ne fordeme.\nNe \u00e6nig man o\u00f0erne ne tyrie ne ne tyne ealles to swy\u00f0e.\nNe \u00e6nig man hine sylfne mid mane ne forswerie.\nNe on leasre gewitnesse \u00e6nig man ne stande.\nNe \u00e6nig man ne gewunie \u00fe\u00e6t he huxlice onhisce, ne \u00f0urh hyrwnesse God ne gegremie.\nNe \u00e6nig man to hlagol sy ne f\u00e6ringa to f\u00e6gen ne eft ne beo to ormod.\nNe \u00e6nig man o\u00feerne b\u00e6ftan ne t\u00e6le ne hyrwe to swy\u00f0e.\nNe \u00e6nig man andan ne healde on his heortan ealles to f\u00e6ste.\nNe \u00e6nig man o\u00f0erne ne hatie to swy\u00f0e.\nNe \u00e6nig man ne gewunie \u00fe\u00e6t he mid yfelum wordum to wyriende weor\u00f0e.\nNe \u00e6nig man ne sy to sacfull ne ealles to geflitgeorn.\nNe \u00e6nig man ne lufige druncen to swy\u00f0e ne fule oferfylle.\nNe \u00e6nig man myrtenes \u00e6fre ne abite ne blodes ne abyrige.\nNe \u00e6nig man wiccecr\u00e6ft \u00e6fre begange.\nNe \u00e6nig man idola weor\u00f0ie \u00e6fre.\nNe \u00e6nig man gemanan wi\u00f0 amansode h\u00e6bbe.\nSunnand\u00e6ges weor\u00f0unge n\u00e6nig man forgyme.\n\u00c6lc man his teo\u00f0unga gel\u00e6ste mid rihte.\nFreolsa & f\u00e6stena healde man georne.\n\u00d0\u00e6t man Gode behate ne aleoge man \u00e6fre.\nNe \u00e6nig man mid unandettan heafodleahtrum husles ne abyrige, ac andette & bete \u00e6r he husel \u00f0icge.\nEac ic l\u00e6re georne mann a gehwilcne \u00fe\u00e6t he his synna andette gelome & mid d\u00e6dbote cl\u00e6nsie hine\nFor\u00f0am, understande se \u00f0e wille, eal hit m\u00e6g to \u00f0earfe, ealswa \u00fe\u00e6t godspel cw\u00e6\u00f0: Penitentiam agite;\nDo\u00f0 d\u00e6dbote eowra synna & eow sona wyr\u00f0 heofona rices duru ra\u00f0e untyned.\nLeofan man, on eornost ic l\u00e6re, cyrra\u00f0 from yfele & fram unrihte & do\u00f0 to gode a swa leng swa mare.\nGyma\u00f0 georne Godes lage & healda\u00f0 hy f\u00e6ste & gelome on gearf\u00e6ce gearwia\u00f0 eow to husle.\nEala, leofan men, ne latia\u00f0 na, ne latia\u00f0, ac ofstlice efsta\u00f0 & to Gode wenda\u00f0.\nAnd se \u00f0e w\u00e6re gitsiende o\u00f0ra manna \u00feinga & \u00e6hta, weor\u00f0e of his agenan rihte begytenan \u00e6lmesgyfa\nSe \u00fee w\u00e6re gifre, weor\u00f0e se syfre; & se \u00f0e w\u00e6re galsere on fulan forligere, weor\u00f0e se cl\u00e6nsere his\nSe \u00fee w\u00e6re weamod, weor\u00f0e se ge\u00feyldmod.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re hohmod, weor\u00f0e se gl\u00e6dmod.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re idelgeorn, weor\u00f0e se notgeorn.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re lofgeorn for idelan weor\u00f0scype, weor\u00f0e se carfull hu he swy\u00feast m\u00e6ge gecweman his\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re ofermod, weor\u00f0e se eadmod.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re sca\u00f0iende, weor\u00f0e se tiligende on rihtlicre til\u00f0e.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re slapol, weor\u00f0e se ful wacor, & se \u00f0e w\u00e6re full slaw, weor\u00f0e se unslaw to cyrican gelome\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re leassagol, weor\u00f0e se so\u00f0sagol.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re b\u00e6cslitol, weor\u00f0e se w\u00e6rsagol.\nSe \u00f0e w\u00e6re stuntwyrde, weor\u00f0e se wiswyrde.\nAnd se \u00f0e on unriht abysgode hine sylfne, se on halgum gebedum abysgie hine symle.\nAnd se \u00f0e w\u00e6re ungeleafful rihtes geleafan, weor\u00f0e se geleafful godcundes rihtes.\n\u00d0us man sceal \u00e6lc unriht mid rihte gebetan & unweod aweodian & god s\u00e6d ar\u00e6ran.\nNu la, leofan men, gelyfa\u00f0 huru georne & anr\u00e6dlice be\u00feenca\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t annes & \u00f0rynnes on godcundnesse\nEalle \u00fea \u00f0ry naman befeh\u00f0 an godcund miht & is untod\u00e6led an ece God, wealdend & wyrhta ealra\nSe is to lufianne & to weor\u00f0ianne ofer ealle o\u00f0re \u00f0ing.\nAnd riht is \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6lc cristen man eac o\u00f0erne lufie & healde mid rihte, & \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6nig o\u00f0rum ne beode\nNe \u00e6nig ne syrwe ne o\u00f0rum ne swicie, ac healde \u00e6lc o\u00f0erne mid rihtre getryw\u00f0e.\nIc l\u00e6re eac georne manna gehwylcne \u00fe\u00e6t he Godes ege h\u00e6bbe \u00e6fre on gemynde & Godes hus symle\nSibbe & some lufie man georne & \u00e6lc fracodlic facn \u00e6fre aweorpe & \u00e6ghwylcne h\u00e6\u00f0enscype wordes\nGodcundre lare folgie man georne & inweardre heortan clypie man to Criste oft & gelome, & cyrican\nRihte teo\u00f0unga gel\u00e6ste man gl\u00e6dlice, & Godes sacerdan hlyste man georne & hy for Godes ege lufige\n\u00c6lmesgedal d\u00e6le man gelome, Mete \u00feam ofhingredum, drenc \u00feam of\u00f0yrstum, hushleow gefarenum,\nWydewan & steopcild werie man & nerie, & \u00f0earfena gehwylcum helpe man georne.\nDomas & dihtas rihte man geornlice, \u00fe\u00e6t leod & lagu trumlice stande.\nBeo manna gehwylc hold & getrywe his worldhlaforde \u00e6fre mid rihte, & beo hlaforda gehwylc milde\nBeo manna gehwylc milde on mode & miltsie for Godes ege, \u00fe\u00e6r he derian m\u00e6ge.\nGodf\u00e6der his godbearn lufie & l\u00e6re & unrihtes styre.\nPater noster & credan mymerian \u00fea yldran & t\u00e6can heora gingran mid rihtan geleafan.\nOn manna gehwylces mode & mu\u00f0e so\u00f0sagu stande.\nOn heortan & on weorcan cl\u00e6nnes gelufie; on ge\u00f0ance & on \u00feeawan syfernes gelicie.\nEac ic l\u00e6re georne manna gehwylcne \u00fe\u00e6t he his luste to swy\u00f0e ne fulgange, ac mid forh\u00e6fednesse oft\nAnd do\u00f0 swa ic l\u00e6re, hyran \u00fea gingran georne heora yldran, & lufian & l\u00e6ran \u00fea yldran heora gingran;\nAnd styre man \u00feam stuntum, & hlyste man \u00feam wisan, & af\u00e6stnie man symle georne on heortan\nOndr\u00e6de man domd\u00e6g & for helle agrise, & ecre reste earnie man georne, & \u00e6ghwylce d\u00e6ge a manna\nEala, hw\u00e6t se bi\u00f0 on worulde wis & ges\u00e6lig \u00fee \u00f0is eal ge\u00f0ence\u00f0 oft & gelome & \u00f0e Godes beboda\nFor\u00f0am God sylfa behet synfullum mannum \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde miltsian, gyf hi woldon earnian.\nEalswa se witega sang & s\u00e6de \u00fea \u00f0a he \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0: Querite Dominum dum inueniri potest, et reliqua.\nItem propheta dicit: In quacumque die peccator conuersus fuerit, et reliqua.\nEt Dominus in euangelio dicit: Gaudium est angelis Dei super, et reliqua.\nEala, leofan men, utan nu efstan & ealle ure lifwegas geornlice rihtan, & ne latian na to lange ne ealles\nAc utan us sylfe mid godan ge\u00feance on worde & on weorce wenian to rihte & geearnian \u00fea myrh\u00f0e\nA sy ecum Gode lof & wyr\u00f0mynt in ealra woruld \u00e6fre butan ende, amen.",
